OVERVIEW OF THE PROJECT / BRIEF INTRODUCTION>

The Supplier evaluation excel macro project aims to automate the process of collecting
evaluation data from multiple suppliers and EPPI related section (excel based) and consolidate
them into a single, structured summary sheet for score calculation and analysis.

---

Benefits:
Efficiency: Eliminates manual copy-paste from multiple sheets.

Accuracy: Reduces human error in tabulation.

Transparency: Provides a clear, centralized summary result.

---

History / Current Situation

Last July 29,2025 EPPI received sudden announcement from SEC that Supplier periodic evaluation
will be handle by EPPI on our own.
SEC system cannot be shared to EPPI, thus EPPI needs to establish our own system/method.
SEC shared the questionnaire forms & Summary Table to compute the result of each supplier

---

Current Challenges with Manual Process

1. Time-Consuming Process
Entering scores and comments from multiple suppliers and end-users takes a lot of time,
especially if there are many criteria and respondents.
Repetitive tasks like copying and pasting increase workload.

2. High Risk of Human Error
Typing mistakes, wrong cell references, or skipped rows can lead to inaccurate evaluations.
Misalignment of data (e.g., entering a score under the wrong supplier) is common.

3. Difficulty in Consolidation
Combining multiple sheets or files manually is prone to duplication or missing data.
Tracking which evaluations are complete becomes challenging.

4. Limited Traceability
Hard to audit changes or identify who entered which data.
No automatic log of updates or corrections.

5. Slow Reporting
Manual tabulation delays the generation of summary result.
Any change requires redoing calculations manually.

---

Proposal

Propose to automate the Supplier Evaluation process with an Excel macro which can:
.Pull data from multiple sheets/files.
·Validate inputs automatically.
·Calculate weighted scores and rankings instantly.
.Generate a centralized summary with one click.





